## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical use of S3 events, Lambda, and DynamoDB with a focus on idempotency and least privilege. The candidate must outline concrete wiring, permissions, and a tangible test plan.

## Key Concepts
- S3 event notifications to Lambda
- CSV parsing and upsert into DynamoDB
- Deduplication via a ProcessedTransactions table (transactionId)
- Least-privilege IAM roles for S3, DynamoDB, CloudWatch
- Test plan: retries, idempotency, rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const s3 = new AWS.S3();
const ddb = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();

exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const bucket = event.Records[0].s3.bucket.name;
  const key = event.Records[0].s3.object.key;
  const obj = await s3.getObject({ Bucket: bucket, Key: key }).promise();
  const lines = obj.Body.toString('utf-8').split('\n');
  for (const line of lines) {
    if (!line.trim()) continue;
    const [transactionId, data] = line.split(',');
    // dedupe check
    const exists = await ddb.get({
      TableName: 'ProcessedTransactions',
      Key: { transactionId }
    }).promise();
    if (exists.Item) continue;
    // write primary record
    await ddb.put({ TableName: 'VendorRecords', Item: { transactionId, data } }).promise();
    await ddb.put({ TableName: 'ProcessedTransactions', Item: { transactionId } }).promise();
  }
  return 'done';
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you add idempotency for partially processed files? 
- How would you test failure rollback without affecting production data?

## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates designing scalable, secure, cross-account data access across tenants with strong isolation and auditable sharing.

## Key Concepts
- Lake Formation catalog-based permissions
- S3 per-tenant prefixes and object ownership
- KMS key policies for residency and encryption
- IAM SCPs and cross-account sharing, data marts

## Code Example
```javascript
// Tenant user policy (pseudo)
{
  'Version': '2012-10-17',
  'Statement': [
    {'Effect': 'Allow', 'Action': ['lakeformation:GrantPermissions', 's3:GetObject'], 'Resource': ['arn:aws:s3:::corp-data/tenant-id-*/**']}
  ]
}

// Data-mart role policy (pseudo)
{
  'Version': '2012-10-17',
  'Statement': [
    {'Effect': 'Allow', 'Action': ['lakeformation:SelectFromDataCatalog'], 'Resource': '*'}
  ]
}

// Cross-account share policy (pseudo)
{
  'Version': '2012-10-17',
  'Statement': [
    {'Effect': 'Allow', 'Action': ['glue:GetTable','s3:GetObject'], 'Resource': ['arn:aws:glue:*:*:catalog','arn:aws:s3:::shared-data/**']}
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor and alert on policy drift?
- What are the trade-offs of using Lake Formation versus direct IAM policies for data access?

